task: actor-receive-fused (channel-callback-allocation's receive half, done right)
agent: okay-42
started: 2026-09-06
branch: feature/actor-receive-fused

why: actor-receive-offer-first measured +19% with an empty mailbox
  and -35% bytes with a full one, and the reason is physical: a failed
  offer reads the producer's OWN cache line, a failed poll reads the
  line the OTHER side writes -- ~17ns, 4000 of them the 67us lost. So
  the try must not be a second scan.

design: (1) Handoff[A] in core -- the callback IS the slot: value,
  filled, waiter, and apply(End) that fills it. One object where
  CanBlock.block allocated a Slot plus a lambda. (2) Channel.receiveInto
  (h): Boolean -- "an element is ready now: write it into h, answer
  true; else register h, answer false". Default: receiveAsync(h);
  false (correct before fast). SentinelChannel: receiveAsync's own
  first scan with an early return on a hit -- no Right(Some(_)), no
  second scan, the miss path byte-identical to today's. (3)
  CanBlock.await(h): park until filled, per platform (JVM/Native; JS
  has no CanBlock). (4) receiveBlocking = Handoff + receiveInto + await
  + h.answer. A hit costs Handoff + Some (was five objects); a miss
  costs Handoff (was two). No cast anywhere: Handoff is typed on A.

measure: actorTell (empty regime) and actorTellBacklog (full regime)
  against channelBuffer, A/B against master, bytes and time; the
  two-regime harness from the declined lane. Expected: -35% bytes
  kept in the full regime, parity or better in the empty one, and
  every receiveBlocking caller in the library allocating less.

laws: TestChannelLaws runs against every implementation and covers
  receiveBlocking; TestPoisonLaws covers the actor loop; new: a
  Handoff suite -- end and failure through the handoff, a synchronous
  end, a parked receiver woken by send, close and fail.
